## 21.13 Owner working agreement — non-developer workflow

The project owner is not expected to write, debug or integrate implementation code manually.

The engineering agent must:

1. Inspect the repository and determine the correct action.
2. Explain the action in plain language.
3. Provide the exact GitHub file path.
4. Provide complete replacement content when a file replacement is needed.
5. Clearly state whether the action is REPLACE, APPEND or CREATE.
6. Never give a patch fragment when a complete file replacement is required.
7. Avoid asking the owner to decide technical architecture that belongs to the developer/architect.
8. Avoid giving local terminal, local worktree or manual Git instructions under the current owner workflow.
9. Never claim a remote save occurred when it did not.
10. Verify the live GitHub file after the owner saves it.

The default working interface remains the owner-controlled GitHub web editor unless the owner changes the operating agreement through the applicable authorized process.

